## 3. Architecture at a glance

```
raw text
   │  tokens_cased / tok            (regex tokenizer, NFKC normalisation, lowercase copy)
   ▼
lowercase tokens ───────────────────────────────────────────────┐
   │                                                            │ original-case tokens kept
   ▼                                                            │ for re-casing at the end
┌──────────────────────── STAGE 1: SpellStage ───────────────────────────┐
│ per DISTINCT token (cached):                                           │
│  1 non-alpha / < 3 chars                -> unchanged                   │
│  2 "dont", "wasnt"...                    -> "don't", "wasn't"  (rule)   │
│  3 unknown word 1 edit from a negation   -> that negation (rule)        │
│  4 CharSpeller (Transformer seq2seq) proposes a word + probability      │
│     accept if dictionary knows it OR model is confident                 │
│     (for already-valid words: only a clearly commoner word, p >= 0.9)   │
│  5 else pyspellchecker suggestion, else unchanged                       │
│  never adds / removes a negation                                        │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
   │ spell-corrected tokens
   ▼
┌──────────────────────── STAGE 2: SentenceTagger ───────────────────────┐
│ char-n-gram bag + word hash per token -> Transformer encoder over the   │
│ WHOLE sentence -> one label per token:                                  │
│   <copy> | <del> | SUF|k|text (edit the ending) | REPL|text (replace)   │
│ apply only if confidence >= tuned threshold (+margin for delete),       │
│ then negation guards                                                    │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
   │ labels
   ▼
apply labels -> restore original capitalisation of untouched words -> detokenize
-> capitalise sentence starts and "I" -> output text
```

Why two stages instead of one network: the two sub-problems have **different data regimes and
different output spaces**.

| | Speller | Tagger |
|---|---|---|
| Question | "What word did they mean?" | "Given a sequence of valid-looking words, which need to change?" |
| Output space | any string up to 20 characters (open) | a small label set per token (closed, but shareable) |
| Context needed | none (word only) | the whole sentence |
| Data available | tens of thousands of word pairs + synthetic | ~2,000 sentence pairs + synthetic |
| Model size | larger | smaller |

