## 15. Troubleshooting checklist

| Symptom | Likely cause | What to do |
|---|---|---|
| First line says `device: cpu` | CPU-only PyTorch build | Install the CUDA build from pytorch.org. |
| `ModuleNotFoundError` | missing package | `pip install pandas numpy rapidfuzz pyspellchecker torch` |
| Speller `val_exact` stuck near 0 | too few real pairs / too little training / learning rate | Check the printed `speller data` line; train longer; try `spell_lr=5e-4`. |
| `grad_norm` → 0 across epochs | vanishing gradients | Lower dropout, check the learning rate; this should be rare with pre-LN. |
| `grad_norm` spikes / loss NaN | instability | Lower `spell_lr`/`tag_lr`; check the data for empty strings. |
| Tagger F0.5 = 0 on every epoch | validation set has no edits, or labels all ignored | Look at the printed class count and "tokens needing an edit"; lower `min_class_count`. |
| Tagger worse than do-nothing | threshold too low / data too small | Raise `copy_loss_weight` toward 1; add more synthetic data; check `target_reachable`. |
| `hybrid_keeps_correct_words` low | speller damages valid words | Raise `rare_accept_prob`, `rare_word_ratio`; add more identity pairs (`synthetic_clean_fraction`). |
| Output loses line breaks / quotes | `detok` simplification | See Limitations. |
| GPU out of memory | batch too large | Lower `spell_batch`, then `ngram_buckets`. |
| Very slow start | single-threaded Python phases | Time them; cache built examples to disk if needed. |
| Cannot load checkpoint | config changed after saving | Checkpoints store their own config; keep the code version that saved them. |

