## 16. Glossary

- **Token:** a word or one punctuation mark, produced by the regex tokenizer.
- **Character n-gram:** a run of `n` consecutive characters (with `<`/`>` boundary markers).
- **Hashing trick:** mapping an unbounded set (all n-grams) to a fixed number of buckets with a hash function.
- **Embedding:** a learned vector looked up from an integer id.
- **Transformer encoder / decoder:** stacks of attention + feed-forward layers; the decoder generates output one character at a time.
- **Teacher forcing:** training the decoder with the *true* previous output characters as input.
- **Greedy decoding:** at each step pick the single most likely next character.
- **Group split:** splitting whole groups (same correct text) between train/val/test.
- **Data leakage:** information from the evaluation data influencing training, making scores too optimistic.
- **Label smoothing:** training toward `(1−ε)·one-hot + ε/K` instead of a pure one-hot target.
- **Calibration:** whether a predicted probability of 0.8 is right about 80% of the time.
- **F0.5:** the F-score that weights precision more than recall.
- **Data processing inequality:** `I(Y;T(X)) ≤ I(Y;X)`; processing cannot create information.
- **Usable (V-)information:** information a given model family can actually extract.
- **Pre-LayerNorm:** normalisation placed inside the residual branch.
- **Vanishing / exploding gradients:** gradients shrinking or growing exponentially with depth during backpropagation.
- **Exposure bias:** a mismatch between training inputs and the inputs seen when the system is used.
